/**
 * Fuse box data for common vehicles.
 * Each vehicle has panels (fuse box locations) with fuses and relays.
 *
 * Structure:
 *   make -> model -> yearRange -> { panels: [...] }
 *
 * Each panel:
 *   - name: Human-readable name (e.g., "Under-Hood Fuse Box")
 *   - location: Physical location description
 *   - fuses: Array of { pos, amps, circuit, desc }
 *   - relays: Array of { pos, circuit, desc }
 *
 * Sources: Toyota/Lexus owner's manuals, NHTSA PDFs, Ford service manuals,
 * Honda owner's manuals, Chevrolet/GM owner's manuals, Mazda owner's manuals,
 * Hyundai/Kia owner's manuals (engine compartment and interior fuse tables),
 * startmycar.com (cross-referenced).
 *
 * Notes:
 *   - Hybrid variants may have additional fuses; the most common gas configuration is covered.
 *   - Amperages may vary slightly between trim levels; the most common value is listed.
 *   - Some positions are unused/spare; only active circuits are listed.
 */

